WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.588 --> 00:00:04.180
Imagine how cool it would be if
we could go back in time and

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:06.840
take classes from the greats?

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:10.510
From Plato, from Maya Angelou,

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:14.050
from Ghandi, from the Wright brothers,
from Einstein.

00:00:14.050 --> 00:00:18.204
Even if half of what they said was wrong,
how much would we have improved as

00:00:18.204 --> 00:00:22.640
humanity to be able to take what they have
learned and be able to build off that?

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:26.561
[CROSSTALK] I've been curious
since day one in my life.

00:00:26.561 --> 00:00:31.010
I got in trouble in school when I
was a kid, asking lots of questions.

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:35.640
I think it's a desire to
understand how the world works and

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:39.780
a realization that life is fragile and
short.

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:41.660
And I want to take advantage of it.

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:43.100
So I've stuttered, I've always stuttered.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:47.760
It was much worse as a kid and I don't
know, I was teased in school about it.

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:53.600
My parents refused to let me use
that as an excuse for anything.

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:57.598
My parents would always insist that when
they had friends over, I would sit with

00:00:57.598 --> 00:01:01.129
them at the dinner table and
I had to participate in the conversation.

00:01:01.129 --> 00:01:03.158
So I was always encouraged.

00:01:03.158 --> 00:01:04.616
Got it.

00:01:04.616 --> 00:01:08.510
At the GSB, I learned about careers and

00:01:08.510 --> 00:01:13.780
areas of business that
I didn't know existed.

00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:17.270
That was really great in
expanding my worldview.

00:01:17.270 --> 00:01:20.150
I think one of the biggest
things I got to just be was,

00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:23.860
I learned what my
comparative advantage was.

00:01:23.860 --> 00:01:27.275
And I learned how to think in ways.

00:01:27.275 --> 00:01:32.834
Yeah, so the story of Masterclass
is one I never expected.

00:01:32.834 --> 00:01:36.017
After going to the GSB,
I tried all different ideas,

00:01:36.017 --> 00:01:38.080
I thought of all different ideas.

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:40.880
And somebody gave me a great constraint.

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:45.860
She said, choose an idea that even if it
fails, you are going to be proud of it.

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:47.150
That was an awesome constraint for me.

00:01:47.150 --> 00:01:50.570
So all the ideas go out
the window except for education.

00:01:50.570 --> 00:01:55.611
Masterclass is a set of online classes
from the absolute best in the world.

00:01:55.611 --> 00:01:59.240
I had to figure out how to go get
the best in the world to actually teach.

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:05.300
I didn't know how to do it and so
I had literally cold email and cold call.

00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:08.585
So the years going by, we aren't
getting any yeses from instructors.

00:02:08.585 --> 00:02:13.918
There were dark days in there
where projected belief but

00:02:13.918 --> 00:02:17.558
unsure and then also when I get a call.

00:02:17.558 --> 00:02:23.141
After we got the first two or three,
it just started to be a chain reaction.

00:02:23.141 --> 00:02:25.276
We ended up launching
with five instructors.

00:02:25.276 --> 00:02:29.048
It was James Patterson, Dustin Hoffman,

00:02:29.048 --> 00:02:33.570
Serena Williams, Usher and
Annie Leibovitz.

00:02:33.570 --> 00:02:36.560
Education is the silver bullet.

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:42.570
The only thing we know as a species
that improves life is education.

00:02:42.570 --> 00:02:47.480
If somebody who never got exposure to the
best in the world all of a sudden now can

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:51.340
learn from the best,
that can only be good for the world.

00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:57.020
There are dark days where you start to
wonder if the critics were actually right.

00:02:57.020 --> 00:03:01.220
And then there are days that
are the highest of highs and

00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:02.760
days you'd never expected.

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:05.230
I don't want to be on my deathbed and
hopefully in a long time and

00:03:05.230 --> 00:03:08.930
think I didn't try to make
the world a tiny bit better.

00:03:08.930 --> 00:03:13.510
I don't think Masterclass would be what
it is today if I hadn't gone to the GSB,

00:03:13.510 --> 00:03:17.140
the things I learned there I still apply.

00:03:17.140 --> 00:03:22.252
It's forced me to believe more in myself,
yeah, and

00:03:22.252 --> 00:03:29.651
believe that I could have more impact
than I ever thought I could have, yeah.

00:03:29.651 --> 00:03:32.214
[MUSIC]

